; A banked program on the BBC Model B+128: lathe/env/bbc.env, run with `*RUN NAME ARGS`, with
; the sideways window $8000-$BFDF switched by lathe/rt/rt_bbc.lth (lathe/docs/bbc.md;
; lathe/docs/boards.md, "The BBC Micro"). The module is the developer's form, which holds RAM
; (the emulator's --bbc-module-ram --bbc-module-scheme direct16), in the slot MODULE_SLOT; the
; program's start-up code loads each bank's file into it from the disc.
;
; This file is the machine. A program, or a test, adds its own `bank`, `place` and `region`
; lines after it (lathe/tests/test_bbc_bank.py does). A bank's value says what it is:
;
;   bank WIN N $8n FILE     bank n (0 to 15) of the module, by convention numbered N = n for
;                           n = 1 to 15 and N = 16 for bank 0 (which the ROM form keeps for its
;                           header and service code); code and constants, and the variables
;                           of the modules placed there (the developer's module is RAM)
;   bank WIN N $0s [FILE]   sideways RAM slot s (0, 1, 12 or 13), by convention N = 20 + s;
;                           regions; a file only if the region has constants
;
; The window ends at $BFDF: the module latches a bank on a read of $BFF0-$BFFF, and a real
; NMOS 6502 reads the byte after a one-byte instruction, so the last 32 bytes are left empty.
; `switch WIN bank farcall` says that no register describes the switch: rt_bbc turns a value
; into the writes of $F4 and ROMSEL and the read of $BFF0+n (configurations.md, "The
; environment file").
cpu       6502
zeropage  $00 $8F
code      $1900 $6BFF
data      $6C00 $7BFF
more      data $0401 $06FF
exit      return $0400  ; the start-up code keeps S at $0400 (bbc.KEEP), and ends with RTS
output    raw
define    BOARD 3       ; the BBC (lathe/host/driver/boards.py)
define    PORTS 2       ; lathe/src/sys.lth over lathe/rt/bbc.lth
define    BBCFS 0       ; file names as given; 1: the DFS's (lathe/rt/bbc/bbcfs.lth)
define    MODULE_SLOT 4 ; the module's slot: rt_bbc.SLOT, and the emulator's --bbc-module-slot
window    WIN $8000 $BFDF
switch    WIN bank farcall
farcall   rt_bbc
